{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"REAL CI FINDING on 2615 PS4 (NOT scanner-integration, NOT flake): pytest ubuntu py3.11 FAILED deterministically (reproduced locally on py3.12). Root cause: 1cef added FixtureHealConfig to the typed Config (_config_schema _SECTION_CLASSES) + reader fixture_heal_interval_days(), but NEVER registered the 'fixture_heal' section in _config_sections._SECTIONS (the coercion+provenance single-source). Consequence: config 'values' had fixture_heal but 'sources'/provenance did not => 3 invariant oracles RED: test_operation_snapshot::test_compose_returns_snapshot_with_values_sources_root_and_version (set(sources)==set(values)), test_mechanism_delta::test_the_committed_baseline_matches_the_live_tree (config_key detector enumerates _SECTIONS, so fixture_heal.interval_days marker-admitted but undetected), and 4x test_config_surface_golden (new live key/env var). FIX (single-source): registered 'fixture_heal':{'interval_days': _as_int minimum=1} in _SECTIONS (mirrors reclaim.horizon_days) + regenerated tests/golden/config_surface.json (adds fixture_heal.interval_days + REBAR_FIXTURE_HEAL_INTERVAL_DAYS). Completes the half-wired section (now first-class: coerced, validated, provenance-tracked, env-overridable). Existing invariants ARE the RED oracle (no new test needed). All 101 config tests GREEN; make lint + typecheck exit 0. Amending -> PS5."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788513687626742001,"uuid":"940a19f1-8968-4d8c-acdd-7fd19c311faa"}